WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.540
Our beaches have always been popular for fishing and white baiting

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.799
and it makes life easier if you can drive your equipment out to your favourite spot.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.780
Under the Northern Pegasus Beach Bylaw that’s still fine

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.300
but there are some rules around vehicles you need to be aware of.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.560
You can only drive on the beach for approved purposes.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:31.140
That includes launching a boat, or transporting equipment for fishing, white baiting or Mahinga Kai.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.500
Here at Kairaki, if you hold a mobility parking permit

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.140
you can also bring your car onto the beach.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.480
But recreational driving, or driving just for pleasure is not allowed

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.780
and neither are two-wheeled motorbikes.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.680
You also need to stick to the designated areas

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:54.560
which are from the Waimakariri River Mouth to the red post located 2.5km north of The Pines Beach

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.860
and from north of the Ashley Rakahuri Estuary up to the Hurunui District boundary.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.700
When driving, stay below the last high-tide mark,

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.900
and give way to people and animals at all times.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.480
You should be going no faster than 30km/h

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.880
and slowing right down to 10km/h when within 50 meters of people.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.180
So it’s not difficult. Keep to the designated areas

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.240
for the approved purposes and drive safely.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.080
We’ve all got a part to play in preserving our beaches &amp; estuary.

